CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 50 namespaced constexpr operator bool resolved: SUCCESS$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^expected constant expression, but got 'operator\(bool\)\(\(const struct integral_constant \*\)&.*'$
--
Companion to `cpp17_constexpr_member_in_template`.  That earlier
test covers constexpr methods of GLOBAL class templates whose
bodies must be eagerly type-checked in their own (class) scope
before being installed at the call site as a non-type template
argument.  This test covers the same pattern when the class
template lives in a NAMESPACE, which prior to the strip-tag fix
in `cpp_instantiate_template.cpp` failed to drain the operator
out of `deferred_typechecking` and surfaced a misleading
"expected constant expression" diagnostic at the use site.
